        <mxCell id="Pr47" value="&lt;b style=&#39;font-size:14px&#39;&gt;Wires crossing each joint&lt;/b&gt;&lt;table style=&#39;font-size:12px;border-collapse:collapse;margin-top:6px&#39;&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;th style=&#39;text-align:left;padding:4px 6px&#39;&gt;Joint&lt;/th&gt;&lt;th style=&#39;padding:4px 6px&#39;&gt;Wires&lt;/th&gt;&lt;th style=&#39;text-align:left;padding:4px 6px&#39;&gt;Cables&lt;/th&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style=&#39;padding:4px 6px;border-top:1px solid #ccc;white-space:nowrap&#39;&gt;&lt;b&gt;J1&lt;/b&gt; base rotation&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&#39;padding:4px 6px;border-top:1px solid #ccc;text-align:center&#39;&gt;&lt;b&gt;26&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&#39;padding:4px 6px;border-top:1px solid #ccc&#39;&gt;J2 lead (3), Gripper lead (3), J6 lead (3), J5 lead (3), J4 lead (3), J3 lead (3), J5 encoder (4), J4 encoder (4)&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style=&#39;padding:4px 6px;border-top:1px solid #ccc;white-space:nowrap&#39;&gt;&lt;b&gt;J2&lt;/b&gt; shoulder&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&#39;padding:4px 6px;border-top:1px solid #ccc;text-align:center&#39;&gt;&lt;b&gt;23&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&#39;padding:4px 6px;border-top:1px solid #ccc&#39;&gt;Gripper lead (3), J6 lead (3), J5 lead (3), J4 lead (3), J3 lead (3), J5 encoder (4), J4 encoder (4)&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style=&#39;padding:4px 6px;border-top:1px solid #ccc;white-space:nowrap&#39;&gt;&lt;b&gt;J3&lt;/b&gt; elbow&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&#39;padding:4px 6px;border-top:1px solid #ccc;text-align:center&#39;&gt;&lt;b&gt;20&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&#39;padding:4px 6px;border-top:1px solid #ccc&#39;&gt;Gripper lead (3), J6 lead (3), J5 lead (3), J4 lead (3), J5 encoder (4), J4 encoder (4)&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style=&#39;padding:4px 6px;border-top:1px solid #ccc;white-space:nowrap&#39;&gt;&lt;b&gt;J4&lt;/b&gt; forearm rotation&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&#39;padding:4px 6px;border-top:1px solid #ccc;text-align:center&#39;&gt;&lt;b&gt;13&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&#39;padding:4px 6px;border-top:1px solid #ccc&#39;&gt;Gripper lead (3), J6 lead (3), J5 lead (3), J5 encoder (4)&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style=&#39;padding:4px 6px;border-top:1px solid #ccc;white-space:nowrap&#39;&gt;&lt;b&gt;J5&lt;/b&gt; wrist tilt&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&#39;padding:4px 6px;border-top:1px solid #ccc;text-align:center&#39;&gt;&lt;b&gt;6&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&#39;padding:4px 6px;border-top:1px solid #ccc&#39;&gt;Gripper lead (3), J6 lead (3)&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style=&#39;padding:4px 6px;border-top:1px solid #ccc;white-space:nowrap&#39;&gt;&lt;b&gt;J6&lt;/b&gt; wrist rotation&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&#39;padding:4px 6px;border-top:1px solid #ccc;text-align:center&#39;&gt;&lt;b&gt;3&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&#39;padding:4px 6px;border-top:1px solid #ccc&#39;&gt;Gripper lead (3)&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontSize=11;" vertex="1" parent="Prcp">
          <mxGeometry x="1180" y="100" width="560" height="330" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="Pr48" value="&lt;b style=&#39;font-size:13px&#39;&gt;Wire colours&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Servo leads&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;font color=&#39;#f39c12&#39;&gt;━━━&lt;/font&gt; signal (PWM) &amp;nbsp; &lt;font color=&#39;#d62728&#39;&gt;━━━&lt;/font&gt; V+ &amp;nbsp; &lt;font color=&#39;#000000&#39;&gt;━━━&lt;/font&gt; GND&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Logic, I²C and encoder cables&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;font color=&#39;#e88b8b&#39;&gt;━━━&lt;/font&gt; 3.3 V &amp;nbsp; &lt;font color=&#39;#000000&#39;&gt;━━━&lt;/font&gt; GND &amp;nbsp; &lt;font color=&#39;#1f6fd1&#39;&gt;━━━&lt;/font&gt; SDA &amp;nbsp; &lt;font color=&#39;#17a2a2&#39;&gt;━━━&lt;/font&gt; SCL&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Supply&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;font color=&#39;#d62728&#39;&gt;━━━&lt;/font&gt; all power (servo supply, servo V+, 5 V to Pi) &amp;nbsp; &lt;font color=&#39;#e88b8b&#39;&gt;━━━&lt;/font&gt; 3.3 V logic &amp;nbsp; &lt;font color=&#39;#000000&#39;&gt;━━━&lt;/font&gt; GND&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Every line is one conductor and is connected to the boxes at both ends, so wires follow when you move a component. Components, wires and background sit on separate layers. Arcs mark where wires cross. Dashed lines mark the joints." style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontSize=11;spacing=10;strokeColor=#aaaaaa;fillColor=#ffffff;rounded=1;" vertex="1" parent="Prcp">
          <mxGeometry x="1180" y="460" width="460" height="250" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="Pr49" value="&lt;b&gt;Notes&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;• Servo leads leave the PCA9685 as one harness and drop off one by one: J1 in the base, J2 beside its servo, J3 at the elbow, then J4 to the gripper up the left side of the forearm.&lt;br&gt;• The J4 encoder cable crosses the servo harness once, just above the elbow, to reach the encoder on the right side.&lt;br&gt;• Base-internal wiring is simplified. The star ground and the OE wire are shown in ers6_wiring_proposed.drawio.&lt;br&gt;• The J3 servo is missing from the STL export, so its position is a guess." style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontSize=11;spacing=10;strokeColor=#aaaaaa;fillColor=#fffbe6;rounded=1;" vertex="1" parent="Prcp">
          <mxGeometry x="1180" y="740" width="460" height="190" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
